        <p>The sale in connection with this WU brought to a close on Saturday night. The total receipts were , ELs. P.S.A.</p>
        <p>The usual weekly meeting held on Sunday wsa presided over by Mr. Jinni/. An ininrestink address was Riven by Mr. J. T. rairh uret, and • couple ot solos were given by Mr. A Bsrson.</p>
        <p>A FORTUNATH EARLIVIVMTN FWITBALLMR</p>
        <p>Or. tfondny, Mr. Tom Wnt.on, Secrotnry of the Liverpool Football Club, came over to Earlextown, and titer so Itersiow with Connie* Wilson. Mittel balfsback for Stock port County,succesded in getting him to sign for Liverpool, on favourable terms. Wilson at one time wne a member of the Earle,- town team, end afterwards of Ilaydock, but tor three seasons bee played for Stockport County. Arc loner 11. EARLICSTOIIN.</p>
        <p>On Motilny night a man named George Holding of lloughton-street, liarlestown, employed in the sanitary department of the Newton Drstrict Coun- cil was seriously injured whilst engaged emptying I Cesspools connected with swine oil cottages situate in Crow-lane. It appears that the man had opened one of the cesspools ready for emptying, and after opening suntan', must have forgotten the Snit one, as in stepping backwards he foil Into the opening. Ile situ found to be injured and after being removed to Dr. Latham's, it was discovered that all hie ribs on One File were staved in. LRCTlltrlfl ON POULTRY K NRPIXO Ar EARLNOTOWN.</p>
        <p>, The third lecture of the course promoted by the Technical I nst ruction Committee on rI. subject of poultry keeping was deloverool by Mr 8r0wn.F.L.4.. on Tuesday evening, in the Town 11•11,Newton. Mr. F. J.WOOOI presoolood, and there waa a moderate at- tendance. The lowure,as hefoore,was illustrated by limelight views.-- Poultry on confinement" was the subject od the fourth and last lecture of the aeries delivered by Mr. Brown in the Town Hall, ikrleatown, on Wednesday evening. Mr.W.Thnrep- am, jun., prmioled in the absence of Mr. W. C wood. At the close. vote of thank, was heartily</p>
        <p>CoLusaa' VIIIPCTN ST COLLINS (AVM</p>
        <p>A strike of collier. and drawers is threatene I at I the Bold and Collins Oreon pits of the Collins Omen I Colliery Company,in consequence of • dispute in connection with what is known as the long draw. Bang. It appear+ the men whose places are some distance away from the rope haulage are dimstisfied with linear piecework prices.alleging that the men who are closet., are in proportion better paid, •nal they mk that they shall be amid at the rate of niatitd. per day. To thin the firm obJect,and consequently the men have individually hamlet in their notice, which will expire on Tuesalny next, SRI they will COAlle v./irk, unless a settlement 111 arrived at in the meantime,</p>
